249
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:20,157
Are you going to duel, Wheeler?

250
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:23,534
Or just stand there like a
loser while I take you apart?

251
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:25,320
I got no choice.

252
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:28,358
All right, I didn't want to do this.

253
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,400
But you got yourself a duel. Are you sure?

254
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:36,740
It's the only way to save
you, so yes. Good answer.

255
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:39,768
I've been waiting for
this moment for years.

256
00:17:40,220 --> 00:17:44,480
As much as I hate this little runt,
I can't let the Orycalcos take him.

257
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,000
No one deserves that.

258
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:51,380
By the way, before my turn
begins, I can play this!

259
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,240
Say, what?

260
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:57,777
Before your turn begins?

261
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:58,690
That's right!

262
00:17:58,773 --> 00:18:00,740
If I have a Gilosaurus in my hand,

263
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:04,237
it automatically jumps to the
field before I make my move!

264
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,520
And I've got two!

265
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,800
So you'll have to deal
with double the dino now!

266
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:11,480
I'm not off to a great start.

267
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,520
So now what?

268
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,680
I'm not finished yet.

269
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,200
I summon Kai-tau-terra.

270
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,110
Aw, man.

271
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:23,057
This guy's already got three monsters
on the field, and I've got Zip.

272
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:27,360
Plus, the seal of Orichalcos makes
my three dinosaurs even stronger.

273
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:34,337
Now that I think about it, you just lucked
out by getting dealt a good opening hand.

274
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:36,477
But you can't win a duel with just luck.

275
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,390
That's funny.

276
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,462
You only beat me last time
because you got lucky.

277
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:41,740
What did you say?

278
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,176
You know he's right.

279
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:46,680
Tristan, whose side are you on anyway?

280
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,648
Just telling it like it is.

281
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:51,337
I think I'll take it easy on you for now

282
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:54,260
and finish up by placing
one card face down.

283
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,840
So let's see what you got.

284
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:02,060
I only have one monster in my hand
that can stand up to his lizards.

285
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:06,220
I summon Panther Warrior and
I'll put him in attack mode.

286
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:12,380
The only problem is,

287
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:16,437
my Panther Warrior can't attack unless
I sacrifice another monster first.

288
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:18,108
So let's see what I can do.

289
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,482
My scapegoats will do the trick.

290
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,689
Alright, I'll place one card
face down and then end my turn.

291
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:31,240
This next in section looks familiar.

292
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,260
It's Cerebone Wasp!

293
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:40,460
My only monster has been infected
by his parasite caterpillar.

294
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:44,000
That means it's no longer
able to defend my life points.

295
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:47,440
Go, my pheromone wasp!

296
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:54,940
You okay?

297
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:56,760
That's not all.

298
00:19:57,100 --> 00:20:00,512
Attacking you directly just
activated his special ability,

299
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:03,337
which means my wasp
allows me to summon any

300
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:06,477
insect monster in my deck
directly to the field.

301
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,980
Then I know just who I'm going to choose.

302
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:12,860
I summon a leech known as Legul!

303
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:23,300
Then I'll activate the
magic card insect barrier!

304
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,877
This barricade provides
the perfect protection

305
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:33,960
against any insect monster
you try and attack with!

306
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:35,590
Huh?

307
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,300
What's he talking about?

308
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:40,364
You don't have any insect
monsters in your deck?

309
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,620
That's not true!

310
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:44,440
Take a closer look at the field, Taya!

311
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:48,260
Your Celtic Guardian's been
contaminated by my parasite,

312
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:51,040
which makes him part insect! No!

313
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:56,320
He's slowly transforming into a new
creature known as Poison Butterfly!

314
00:20:56,640 --> 00:21:00,340
And even though it has
2,700 attack points,

315
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,660
it can't hurt me thanks
to my insect barrier!

316
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:08,560
And since it can't attack or
defend, it's virtually useless!

317
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:13,517
Weevil is a much stronger
duelist than I remember,

318
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,835
now that he's infused with
the power of the Ori Kalkos.

319
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:22,600
He seems unstoppable, but I refuse to let
him stand in the way of rescuing Yugi.

320
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,860
Alright, my move!

321
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:35,017
It won't be long now The soul of the

322
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:38,780
pharaoh is nearly in my grasp After all,

323
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:41,520
we have the perfect bait
